# Synthetic full two-line draft; not admitted or executable.
Choreoform authoring "0.18.0".
Process "Order fulfillment".
Start at "Start acceptance".
Inputs ["Order" uses "Original order"]. Outputs ["First line" uses "First line disposition", "Second line" uses "Second line disposition"]. Outcomes ["recorded"].
Use cancellation "Customer cancellation", faults "Unhandled faults", closure "Preserve order obligations" and races "Order commitments".
Require actor "Customer" under "Customer authority".
Rule for actor "Customer authority". Permit when (((the fact "roles") contains ("order.customer")) and ((the fact "relationships") contains ("order.submitter"))). End policy.
Require actor "Commerce operator" under "Commerce operator authority".
Rule for actor "Commerce operator authority". Permit when ((the fact "roles") contains ("order.commerce")). End policy.
Require actor "Warehouse operator" under "Warehouse operator authority".
Rule for actor "Warehouse operator authority". Permit when ((the fact "roles") contains ("order.warehouse")). End policy.
Require actor "Support agent" under "Support agent authority".
Rule for actor "Support agent authority". Permit when ((the fact "roles") contains ("order.support")). End policy.
Require actor "Clock observer" under "Clock observer authority".
Rule for actor "Clock observer authority". Permit when ((the fact "roles") contains ("order.clock")). End policy.
Require actor "Keep order deadlines fixed" under "No deadline extension".
Rule for actor "No deadline extension". Permit when (false). End policy.
Rule for protection "Order access". Permit access when ((the fact "purpose") equals ("fulfillment")). End policy.
Rule for settlement "Settle children". Unfinished work cancel. End policy.
Rule for cancel "Stop work". Authority "Commerce operator". For children use "Settle children". End policy.
Rule for cancel "Customer cancellation". Authority "Customer". For children use "Settle children". End policy.
Rule for faults "Unhandled faults". Handle empty. End policy.
Rule for closure "Ordinary close". Fully terminal. End policy.
Rule for race "Acceptance order". Accept in acceptance order. End policy.
Rule for closure "Preserve order obligations". Reconcile in "Order settlement". End policy.
Rule for race "Order commitments". Guard commits when ((not ((field "line ID" of (field "first line" of (the representation of (the value of "Original order")))) equals (field "line ID" of (field "second line" of (the representation of (the value of "Original order")))))) and ((field "amount" of (the representation of (the value of "Original order"))) equals ((field "amount" of (field "first line" of (the representation of (the value of "Original order")))) plus (field "amount" of (field "second line" of (the representation of (the value of "Original order"))))))). End policy.
Protect data as "Order information". Under "Order access". Sensitivity "order". Purposes ["Order fulfillment"]. Participants ["Customer", "Commerce operator", "Warehouse operator", "Support agent", "Clock observer"]. Capabilities ["Reserve first line", "Reserve second line", "Authorize order payment", "Release first reservation", "Release second reservation", "Void authorization", "Pack first line", "Pack second line", "Purchase first label", "Purchase second label", "Hand over first parcel", "Hand over second parcel", "Observe first delivery", "Observe second delivery", "Stop first warehouse work", "Stop second warehouse work", "Void first label", "Void second label", "Capture committed amount", "Refund captured amount", "Request first intercept", "Request second intercept", "Notify customer of order", "Release first reservation during settlement", "Release second reservation during settlement"]. End protection.
Describe type "Order instruction" as record with ["order" as type "Order" from "Order types", "scope key" as text, "scope revision" as text, "request revision" as text, "amount" as decimal with 2 places, "currency" as text, "basis reference" as text, "address revision" as text, "target quantity" as optional whole number, "target warehouse" as optional text].
